<task id="002" project="smart-todo-r5">
  <metadata>
    <title>Hoist 13-file rich Kanban subtree into @spaarke/smart-todo-components (FR-01)</title>
    <phase>1: Shared-lib foundation</phase>
    <gate>001 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Moves 13 files (~4,100 LOC) across a package boundary, requires re-homing multiple LW-local hook/service dependencies to stay host-agnostic, and is on the critical path for every downstream FR-02/03/05..15 task. Architecture-adjacent change to a shared library consumed by 2+ hosts.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>High-blast-radius: this is the core hoist of the project — an incoherent or partial move breaks `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components`'s build for every consumer (LegalWorkspace today, future SpaarkeAi Direct widget). The 13 files have non-trivial LW-local dependencies (hooks, services, types) that must be resolved host-agnostically without duplicating or drifting from the locked scoring contract.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Same package (`Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components`) and same LW-local source tree as tasks 001 (prerequisite) and 003 (immediate successor) — this is a serial spine (001→002→003), not a parallelizable task.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>001</deps>
    <tags>react, typescript, shared-lib, refactor</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Move the 13-file rich Kanban subtree from `src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/components/SmartToDo/` (`KanbanCard.tsx`, `KanbanHeader.tsx`, `AddTodoBar.tsx`, `DismissedSection.tsx`, `ThresholdSettings.tsx`, `TodoAISummaryDialog.tsx`, `TodoDetailPane.tsx`, `PriorityScoreCard.tsx`, `EffortScoreCard.tsx`, `SmartToDo.tsx`, `SmartToDoDialog.tsx`, `todoScoringTypes.ts`, `index.ts`) INTO `@spaarke/smart-todo-components` (`src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/`), making them host-agnostic (zero imports reaching into `src/solutions/...`), using ONLY the clean `@spaarke/ui-components/...` package-specifier import pattern restored by task 001 for any UI.Components imports (never the relative-path bypass). Preserve bit-for-bit scoring parity against the existing locked `todoScoring.ts` contract in the target package — do not change the composite score formula or weights.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in React component extraction/hoisting, host-agnostic peer-package design, and TypeScript module boundaries. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>The 13 hoisted components/types are present under `src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/` (organized per the package's existing `components/` / `types/` conventions), exported from the package's public surface (`src/index.ts` and/or `src/components/index.ts`), with zero import reaching into `src/solutions/...` anywhere in the moved files; the package builds (`tsc --noEmit`); `todoScoring.ts`-driven score output is bit-for-bit identical to pre-hoist for the same inputs.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-01 names this exact 13-file list as the hoist target, following "the R4-102 host-agnostic parity pattern" — the precedent set by `useKanbanColumns.ts`, which was hoisted in R4 task 101 into this same package and kept host-agnostic via structural typing (`IKanbanTodoLike`) rather than importing LegalWorkspace's concrete `ITodo` type. This task is the SAME kind of move for the richer Kanban UI subtree. Investigation confirms `src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/components/SmartToDo/SmartToDo.tsx` (805 LOC, the largest file in the set) currently imports LW-local hooks/services directly: `useTodoItems`, `useKanbanColumns` (the LegalWorkspace-local version — distinct from the already-hoisted `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/hooks/useKanbanColumns.ts`), `useUserPreferences`, `useFeedTodoSync`, `DataverseService`, `types/entities` (`ITodo`), `utils/todoScoreUtils`, `types/enums`, `types/xrm`. These MUST be resolved host-agnostically (props injection, structural typing, or a host-service-interface pattern mirroring `IFeedSyncBridge`/`IKanbanDataverseService` already in the package) — NOT smuggled in via a `src/solutions/...` import. `todoScoringTypes.ts` and the package's existing `utils/todoScoring.ts` are the locked scoring contract; do not duplicate or diverge from it.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/components/SmartToDo/KanbanCard.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/components/SmartToDo/KanbanHeader.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/components/SmartToDo/AddTodoBar.tsx</file>
