      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/widgets/SmartTodoWidget/SmartTodoWidget.tsx</file>
      <file>src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sections/todo.registration.ts</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="R4-102 host-agnostic hoist precedent" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/hooks/useKanbanColumns.ts">Structural typing (`IKanbanTodoLike`) + optional injected service (`IKanbanDataverseService`, inert no-op when omitted) — the established way this package hoists LW-coupled logic without importing LW types directly. Apply the same shape to `SmartToDo.tsx`'s LW-local hook/service dependencies.</pattern>
      <pattern name="host-brokers-coupling shim" location="src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sections/todo.registration.ts">The existing `SmartTodoWidget` consumer shows the target end-state: the shared-lib component is host-agnostic; the LW-side shim (`FeedSyncBridgeHost`) owns all LW-specific coupling (FeedTodoSyncContext, BroadcastChannel, Xrm.Navigation) and passes it in via typed props/callbacks.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare rigor level per CLAUDE.md §8; load ADR-012, ADR-021, spec.md, CLAUDE.md, and the `useKanbanColumns.ts` + `todo.registration.ts` canonical references before touching any file.</step>
    <step order="1">Read all 13 LW-local files fully; catalogue every import that reaches into `src/solutions/...` (hooks, services, types) per file — this is the dependency inventory that drives the host-agnostic redesign.</step>
    <step order="2">For each LW-local dependency identified, decide the host-agnostic resolution: (a) prop injection if the caller already has the data/callback, (b) an optional injected service interface mirroring `IKanbanDataverseService`/`IFeedSyncBridge` if it's a data-access dependency, or (c) a locally-duplicated PURE type/util already covered by the package's existing `types/todo.ts` or `utils/todoScoring.ts` (verify no duplication of the locked scoring contract).</step>
    <step order="3">Move `todoScoringTypes.ts` first (types only, likely zero LW dependencies) into `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/types/`, reconciling with the existing `types/todo.ts` (no duplicate type definitions).</step>
    <step order="4">Move the leaf presentational components with the fewest dependencies first (`KanbanCard.tsx`, `KanbanHeader.tsx`, `PriorityScoreCard.tsx`, `EffortScoreCard.tsx`, `ThresholdSettings.tsx`) into `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/components/`, rewriting their imports per the step-2 plan.</step>
    <step order="5">Move the mid-tier components (`AddTodoBar.tsx`, `DismissedSection.tsx`, `TodoAISummaryDialog.tsx`, `TodoDetailPane.tsx`, `SmartToDoDialog.tsx`).</step>
    <step order="6">Move `SmartToDo.tsx` last (the largest, most-coupled file) — apply the host-agnostic redesign from step 2 for its LW-local hook/service dependencies.</step>
    <step order="7">Create/update `index.ts` in the hoisted location exporting all 13 components + their prop types, and update `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/index.ts` (and/or `src/components/index.ts`) to re-export them from the package's public surface.</step>
    <step order="8">Delete the original 13 files from `src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/components/SmartToDo/` ONLY after task 003 (the shim conversion) confirms the shim consumes the package cleanly — coordinate the deletion timing with task 003; this task may leave the LW-local files in place temporarily if task 003 is not run in the same session, but MUST NOT leave the LW-local files as the compiled source of truth once both tasks complete.</step>
    <step order="9">Run `npm run build` (`tsc --noEmit`) in `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components`; fix any type errors from the move.</step>
    <step order="10">Grep the hoisted files for `src/solutions` to confirm zero reach-in imports remain.</step>
    <step order="11">Verify scoring parity: compare computed scores for a representative set of inputs against pre-hoist `todoScoreUtils.ts` output (or existing unit test fixtures) to confirm bit-for-bit match with the package's `todoScoring.ts`.</step>
    <step order="12">Update `projects/smart-todo-r5/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: mark 002 status 🔲 → ✅.</step>
    <step order="13">Document any deviation (e.g., a dependency that could not be cleanly resolved host-agnostically) in `projects/smart-todo-r5/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any of the 13 LW-local components has a hard dependency on LegalWorkspace app state (e.g., a React Context provider, a singleton service, or global app config) that cannot be made host-agnostic via prop injection or an optional service interface, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than smuggling the app coupling into the shared lib via a disguised import or a `src/solutions/...` reach-in.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021) — hoisted KanbanCard">
      <steps>
        <step>Render the hoisted `KanbanCard` in a harness or Storybook with `webLightTheme`.</step>
        <step>Switch to `webDarkTheme`.</step>
        <step>Verify background, urgency-accent, badge, and text colors adapt via semantic tokens with no hardcoded values.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All colors adapt without any hex/rgb literals per ADR-021; no visual regression vs. the pre-hoist LW-local `KanbanCard`.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Visual parity — full Kanban subtree">
      <steps>
        <step>Render the hoisted `SmartToDo` component with representative sample data in the package's test harness.</step>
        <step>Compare against a screenshot/description of the pre-hoist LW-local rendering.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Pixel-equivalent layout and content; no missing icons, badges, or interactive affordances.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build + type-check `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components`</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run grep to verify no `src/solutions` reach-in remains; run file-move commands</tool>
  </tools>

