  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the hoist is complete, when `import { SmartToDo, KanbanCard, ... } from '@spaarke/smart-todo-components'` is used, then all 13 hoisted symbols (+ their exported prop types) resolve from the package's public surface.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a repo-wide grep for `src/solutions` scoped to the hoisted files, when run after this task, then zero matches remain.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the package builds (`tsc --noEmit`), when run, then it succeeds with zero errors.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given identical To Do input data, when the composite score is computed pre- vs. post-hoist, then the numeric output is bit-for-bit identical (no formula/weight drift).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no hex/rgb literal or inline color is introduced anywhere in the moved files (grep-verified per ADR-021).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no LW Context provider, singleton service, or `src/solutions/...` import is smuggled into the hoisted files — every LW dependency is resolved via prop injection or an optional service interface.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec section: FR-01. Step 2 of the Phase 1 serial spine (001→002→003). The `SmartTodo` Code Page (`src/solutions/SmartTodo/src/components/SmartToDo.tsx`) has its OWN separate, unrelated local component of a similar name — it is NOT part of this hoist's scope; do not confuse the two. If time allows, note the potential duplication as a deferral candidate (`/project-defer-issue-tracking`) but do not act on it in this task.</notes>

